# Mooldir time-synchronisation policy (KZ certification FIB §44 / OSI §2.6 / §4.5)
#
# Mooldir requires that the host clock be synchronised to UTC(kz), the
# Kazakhstan national time scale. Approved upstream servers:
#
#   primary:    time.kz
#   secondary:  time1.kazntp.kz
#   secondary:  time2.kazntp.kz
#
# Permitted maximum drift: ±500 ms from the upstream.
# Permitted unreachable-window: 60 minutes (after which alerts must fire).
#
# Implementation responsibilities:
#
#   1. Host or orchestrator runs chrony (or equivalent) pointed at the
#      servers above. For Railway-hosted Mooldir, see runbook
#      `docs/deployment-hardening.md` — Railway uses upstream NTP from the
#      cloud provider; we additionally pin chrony in the bare-metal
#      hardening profile.
#
#   2. The Mooldir API records `mooldir.clock.drift_ms` as an OTel gauge
#      every 60s via the `tasks/clockDriftMonitor.ts` job. Drift > 500 ms
#      OR an "unreachable" status >= 60 min raises a `critical` alert per
#      FIB §1.
#
#   3. On startup, the API process logs the result of
#      `date -u` + `chronyc tracking` (when chrony is installed) so the
#      auditor can confirm UTC(kz) sync.
#
# Reviewing auditor: confirm the host is running chrony or equivalent and
# that the upstream is one of the approved servers above. The aspect of
# "national scale UTC(kz)" in ППРК ЕТ п.139 is satisfied by time.kz, which
# is operated by the National Institute of Metrology of the Republic of
# Kazakhstan.
